     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><font color=\"#5856d6\"><span>it looks to me that all the model is fitting well.</span></font></div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>Correct, the chi-squared test does not reject the null hypothesis of exact fit in the population.</div><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><span style=\"color:rgb(88,86,214)\">What indices should I report in a paper?</span></div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>Chi-squared is enough, but most journals prefer reporting at least 2 other measures of fit (e.g., RMSEA, CFI, and/or SRMR are the most common).  </div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1207/S15328007SEM0703_6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1207/S15328007SEM0703_6&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792424882615000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3AXQgTI2H5A4PSPtLRHkhS\">https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1207/S15328007SEM0703_6</a><br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\"><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792424882615000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2QTrws9L4-8-d-YG2foiWx\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
